Decided: one Logs::rotate (copy then truncate in place) serves cooee.log, terminal.log and perf.log, run at start and every 10 minutes
Because: "One rotation function serves all three."
Decided: farm at the index's commit installs from bytes compiled into the build; any other pack is a depth-1 sparse fetch of its folder into <data>/themes/<name>/
Because: q1616
Decided: on start an old <data>/themes/<name>.git is deleted only after its new form is fetched; an unfetchable one stays and is retried next start
Because: "only once the new form is in place"
Rejected: renaming the logs instead of copy+truncate — launchd's stdout and the perf writer hold the file open and would keep writing to the rotated file
Rejected: running the migration on the live mini data folder from the lane — it deletes owner data; measured on a copy of it instead
Check: kitchen's clone is shallow with only packs/kitchen checked out (tests/themes.rs an_index_pack_is_a_shallow_clone_of_its_folder_alone)
Owner: Logs stop growing past 16 MB each, and themes take under 1 MB instead of 123 MB; farm works offline on first run.
